  <data name="Docs.Files.Intro" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>A theme is a text file ending in &lt;code&gt;.theme&lt;/code&gt;. Save it in &lt;code&gt;~/.config/hackeros/themes/&lt;/code&gt; for yourself; an administrator can copy it to &lt;code&gt;/etc/hackeros/themes/&lt;/code&gt; for every user. The file is also the export: copy it, send it, open it here.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Docs.Files.Platforms" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>&lt;code&gt;platforms&lt;/code&gt;: &lt;code&gt;desktop&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;mobile&lt;/code&gt; or both. On a form factor the base theme does not style, the tokens apply over that form factor's default theme.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Docs.Files.Tokens" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Only the tokens below are read, and each value is checked against its type. An invalid line is ignored with a warning; there is no free CSS, no remote font or image and no script.</value>
